om/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fwbjee%2F2019_che_a42.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fwbjee%2F2019_che_a42.png?alt=media\">\r\nSo, the option (a) is correct answer.","difficulty":"Easy","source":"WBJEE 2019","_marksId":"64a8145de0ff5a5425a85af7"},{"id":117966,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Carboxylic Acid Derivatives","exam":"Engineering","examName":"WBJEE","q":"The compound, which evolves carbon dioxide on treatment with aqueous solution of sodium bicarbonate at $25^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C},$ is","options":["$\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\mathrm{H}_{5} \\mathrm{OH}$","$\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{COCl}$","$\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CONH}_{2}$","$\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{OOOC}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{5}$"],"answer":1,"solution":"$\\mathrm{CH}_{3}-\\mathrm{C}O-\\mathrm{Cl}$ hydrolyses to form $\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{COOH}$\r\neven at $25^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C},$ which subsequently reacts with $NaHCO_{3}$ (sodium bicarbonate) present in the same medium to form carbon dioxide $\\left(\\mathrm{CO}_{2}\\right)$.\r\nThe reaction involved is given below. $\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{COCl}+\\mathrm{NaHCO}_{3} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{COONa}+\\mathrm{HCl}+\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$\r\nThus, the option (b) is correct answer.","difficulty":"Easy","source":"WBJEE 2019","_marksId":"64a8145ee0ff5a5425a85af9"},{"id":117967,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Carboxylic Acid Derivatives","exam":"Engineering","examName":"WBJEE","q":"The ease of hydrolysis in the compounds $\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{COCl}(\\mathrm{I}), \\mathrm{CH}_{3}-\\mathrm{CO}-\\mathrm{O}-\\mathrm{COCH}_{3}(\\mathrm{II})\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{COOC}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{5}(\\mathrm{III})$ and $\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CONH}_{2}$ (IV) is of\r\nthe order","options":["$I\\gt II\\gt III\\gt IV$","$IV\\gt III\\gt II\\gt I$","$I\\gt II\\gt IV\\gt III$","$II\\gt I\\gt IV\\gt III$"],"answer":0,"solution":"The ease of hydrolysis of carbonyl compounds depend on the group attached to the carbonyl carbon. Among the given options, chlorine $(-$ Cl) group is clectron withdrawing group which makes the carbonyl group electrophilic. Hence, hydrolysis can occur most easily. The order for electron withdrawing tendency among given options is as follows:\r\n\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\n-\\mathrm{Cl}>-\\mathrm{OCOCH}_{3}>-\\mathrm{OC}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{5}>-\\mathrm{NH}_{2} \\\\\\end{array}$\r\nSo, the correct order for the ease of hydrolysis in the given compounds is as follows:\r\n$\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{COCl}>\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{COOCOCH}_{3}>\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{COOC}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{5}>\\mathrm{CH}_{3}{\\mathrm{IV}} \\mathrm{CONH}_{2}","difficulty":"Medium","source":"WBJEE 2018","_marksId":"64a8144de0ff5a5425a85a5e"},{"id":117968,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Carboxylic Acid Derivatives","exam":"Engineering","examName":"WBJEE","q":"Identify $'M'$ in the following sequence of reactions\r\n<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fwbjee%252F2018_che_q47.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fwbjee%2F2018_che_q47.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fwbjee%2F2018_che_q47.png?alt=media\">","options":["<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fwbjee%252F2018_che_q47_opta.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fwbjee%2F2018_che_q47_opta.png?alt=media\"