\r\nreaction.<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fwbjee%252F2018_che_a47c.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fwbjee%2F2018_che_a47c.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fwbjee%2F2018_che_a47c.png?alt=media\">\r\nIn this reaction, migration of an alkyl or aryl group takes place from carbonyl carbon of the amide to the $\\mathrm{N}$ -atom. So, $\\mathrm{C}_{8} \\mathrm{H}_{8} \\mathrm{Cl}$ NO must be an amide with structural formula.<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fwbjee%252F2018_che_a47d.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fwbjee%2F2018_che_a47d.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fwbjee%2F2018_che_a47d.png?alt=media\">","difficulty":"Medium","source":"WBJEE 2018","_marksId":"64a8144de0ff5a5425a85a61"},{"id":117969,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Carboxylic Acid Derivatives","exam":"Engineering","examName":"WBJEE","q":"The correct order of acid strengths of benzoic acid $(X),$ peroxybenzoic acid $(Y)$ and $p$-nitrobenzoic acid $(Z)$ is","options":["$Y\\gt Z\\gt X$","$Z\\gt Y\\gt X$","$Z\\gt X\\gt Y$","$Y\\gt X\\gt Z$"],"answer":2,"solution":"$\\because$ In $p$ -nitrobenzoic acid $(Z)-\\mathrm{NO}_{2}$ present as electron withdrawing group, thus is most acidic\r\n<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0